<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sejong the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1397–1450</span> · Also known as King Sejong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sejong the Great was the fourth king of Joseon <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, ruling from 1418 to 1450. He supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hall-of-worthies">Hall of Worthies</a>, a royal research institute, and under him Korea created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hangul">Hangul</a> alphabet, rain gauges, water clocks and new works on agriculture and medicine. His reign also fixed Korea's northern border on the Yalu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tumen">Tumen</a> rivers.</p></div>
